# 🐳 8️⃣ Catalog Service

## Database Configuration

Catalog originally attempted to connect to:

```text
127.0.0.1:5432
```

Inside a Docker container, `127.0.0.1` refers to the **container itself**, not the EC2 host.

Correct configuration:

```text
host.docker.internal:5432
```

Check the application configuration:

```bash
grep -n -E "DATABASE|DB_|postgres|5432|process.env" \
services/catalog-service/main.go
```

Environment variable:

```text
CATALOG_DB_DSN
```

## Start Catalog

```bash
docker rm -f catalog-service 2>/dev/null

docker run -d \
  --name catalog-service \
  --network microservices-net \
  --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway \
  -e CATALOG_DB_DSN="postgres://microapp:microapp123@host.docker.internal:5432/catalog_db?sslmode=disable" \
  -p 8082:8082 \
  devops-shack/catalog-service:1.0
```

Verify:

```bash
docker ps
docker logs catalog-service
```

Check environment:

```bash
docker inspect catalog-service \
  --format '{{json .Config.Env}}'
```

