# 🔍 🔟 Discover Remaining Services

Before starting the remaining services, inspect their actual configuration instead of guessing environment variable names.

```bash
grep -R -n -E \
"127.0.0.1:5432|localhost.*5432|process.env|DB_URL|DB_DSN|DATABASE_URL" \
services/ 2>/dev/null
```

Determine the following for every service:

| Service      | Database          | Environment Variable | Port   |
| ------------ | ----------------- | -------------------- | ------ |
| Catalog      | `catalog_db`      | `CATALOG_DB_DSN`     | `8082` |
| Inventory    | `inventory_db`    | `INVENTORY_DB_URL`   | `8083` |
| Notification | `notification_db` | Verify source        | Verify |
| Auth         | `auth_db`         | Verify source        | Verify |
| Order        | `order_db`        | Verify source        | Verify |
| Payment      | `payment_db`      | Verify source        | Verify |
| Analytics    | `analytics_db`    | Verify source        | Verify |
| Frontend     | N/A               | Verify configuration | Verify |

